  "id": "a-b-design",
  "term": "A-B design",
  "definition": "An A-B design is a study approach used when a new policy or intervention is introduced and its effects are examined by comparing what happened before the change with what happened after it. In the source context, it is presented as a practical option when randomization, delaying the intervention, or blinding are not ethically or legally feasible.",
